    "title_es": "Cuentos de la selva",
    "title_lt": "Jungle Tales",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "lt": "Horacio Quiroga (1878–1937) was born in Uruguay, but he lived for many years in Misiones, in the jungle of northern Argentina, near the Paraná River. There he told his children stories about the animals of the jungle, and in 1918 he published them in a book: “Cuentos de la selva.” In the book, turtles, parrots, caimans, and stingrays talk. But these are not sweet stories: the jungle is real, hot, and dangerous, and the animals are clever, loyal, and sometimes cruel. Today it is read in schools all over Latin America. The short sentences, the clear images, and the warm humor make the reading easy and enjoyable.",
